course: dictionary
lesson: 1845
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Cockeyed is an informal word with three meanings, and the sentences around it show you which one to choose. «The picture on the wall was cockeyed, so I straightened it.» The clue is straightened, so cockeyed means crooked, not level.
explain: «That was a cockeyed plan, and it fell apart in five minutes.» The clue is plan, and a plan that falls apart quickly is not sensible. Here cockeyed means silly. Always check: does your meaning fit the sentence?
explain: The third meaning is old-fashioned and can be unkind, so people rarely use it now. «The cockeyed squid has one big eye that looks up and one small eye that looks down.» The eyes point in different directions, so this meaning is cross-eyed.
fact: Cockeyed is an informal word, so you hear it in everyday talk and stories more than in formal writing.
fact: «Cockeyed» means crooked or not level, as in «knocked cockeyed».
fact: «Cockeyed» can also mean silly or not sensible, as in «a cockeyed idea».
fact: «Cockeyed» (old-fashioned, can be unkind) means having eyes that look in different directions, which is cross-eyed.
fact: To choose the right meaning, look at the sentence: a picture, hat or shelf that is crooked, an idea that is silly, or eyes that point different ways.
exercise: «The picture on the wall was cockeyed.» What does cockeyed mean here? | *Crooked, not straight | Silly and foolish | Very bright and colourful | Tired and sleepy
exercise: Ella says, «That was a cockeyed plan.» What does it suggest? | A plan that was finished early | *A plan that was silly or not sensible | A plan that was very neat and careful | A plan made from wood
exercise: «The cockeyed squid has one big eye that looks up and one small eye that looks down.» What does cockeyed mean in this sentence? | *Having eyes that look in different directions | Crooked and not level | Swimming very fast | Glowing in the dark
test: Mum says the shelf is knocked cockeyed. What does it mean? | Clean and shiny | *Crooked, not level | Noisy and loud | Empty and light
test: Which meaning of cockeyed is old-fashioned and can be unkind? | Informal and friendly | Silly or not sensible | *Cross-eyed | Crooked or not level
exam: Jayden says, «Your cockeyed idea will never work.» What does cockeyed mean here? | Cross-eyed | Shiny | *Silly or not sensible | Crooked
